# What must never end up inside the data-server image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file every `docker build`
# of this directory would bake in
#
#   * `.env` — the local POSTGRES_PASSWORD, KC_ADMIN_PASSWORD and the
#     framework API key,
#   * `backups/` — database dumps containing case data,
#   * and, with tarball releases, the PREVIOUS release image (doubling
#     the image size).
#
# Nobody would see it. The image runs correctly either way, the files sit
# unused next to the code, and the only symptom is that every recipient
# of the image receives the operator's secrets and somebody else's case data.
#
# The image needs `app/`, `main.py` and `requirements.txt`. Everything
# else in this directory is operator-side tooling.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backups/
agent-image-*.tar.gz
dist/
.dist-stage*
keycloak/import/

# Operator tooling — the customer receives these as downloads from
# /agent/, not baked into the image they run.
install.sh
update.sh
backup.sh
docker-compose*.yml
Caddyfile.template
version.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

